Prepare an automobile for refinishing by:
- assessing imperfections on the automobile and ensuring the surface of the automobile is cleaned with a quality wax and grease remover;
- analyzing the type of paint, previous and current damage such as flaking, peeling, cracking and repainting, rust, damage from acids and other effects of oxidation;
- featheredging all broken edges, sanding, rough masking, body filling scratches;
- priming all bare metal areas by removing waves in body work and repriming areas as needed; and,
- selecting and applying colour coats using a spray paint booth.

Explain the responsibility of buyers when purchasing automobiles, including:
- the legal implications of purchasing new or used automobiles;
- factors to consider when selecting appropriate automobiles to meet specific needs/wants;
- evaluating an automobile’s condition;
- types of warranty (e.g., limited, extended, manufacturer’s) available to the purchaser;
- options of purchasing or leasing automobiles;
- recertification when purchasing tagged automobiles; and,
- implications of “buyer beware” (e.g., stolen automobile, eligible for registration, liens against an automobile, automobile history).

